ssage, line, then the error it becomes, class, message, line,"] [198 1 "// offset, end line, end offset, text, joined by \\x02; then \\x03) and gives the answer: PyErr_WarnExplicitObject at"] [199 1 "// the warning's line, a warning a filter turns into an error the reader's SyntaxError (_PyTokenizer_parser_warn,"] [200 1 "// warn_invalid_escape_sequence: the parse ends there, queue 228)."] [233 4 "// _PyPegen_number_token: a decimal literal over sys.set_int_max_str_digits's limit, which is the run's: the"] [234 4 "// reader records the digits of one past the lowest limit (p[1]) and the error's location"] [244 21 "// a compiler's warning: PyErr_ProgramTextObject's line"] [255 1 "// compileModuleName is 3.15's compile(..., module=NAME) while that compile runs (nil: none): the warnings' module"] [256 1 "// (_PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning's PyErr_WarnExplicitObject(..., module, NULL); queue 239)"] [259 1 "// emitCompileWarnings is _PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning for each of the compiler's warnings, in order:"] [260 1 "// warnings.warn_explicit(msg, SyntaxWarning, file, line); a SyntaxWarning a filter turns into an error becomes"] [261 1 "// the SyntaxError of its location, the compile's result."] [307 1 "// isIncomplete reports an interactive statement that needs more lines (codeop's incomplete input):"] [308 1 "// (PY7: a fresh _IncompleteInputError each time, isIncomplete tells it)"] [324 4 "// 3.15 (queue 239): _PyEval_LazyImportName, unless the compiler forced the import eager"] [359 1 "// eagerImportName is IMPORT_NAME's eager import (_PyEval_ImportName): builtins.__import__ called, or the runtime's."] [366 3 "// builtins.__import__ replaced: called as CPython's import_name calls it"] [387 4 "// a mapping's namespace (a dict subclass's, exec's mapping; queue 219): the names stored through it"] [401 1 "// builtinImportFn is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [404 1 "// isBuiltinImport is whether o is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [407 1 "// builtinImport is __import__(n